Wonderful.

58
00:04:03,900 --> 00:04:05,680
That was nice work out there now.

59
00:04:07,060 --> 00:04:07,980
Thanks, Yuki.

60
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:10,300
Honestly, you did a great job.

61
00:04:11,300 --> 00:04:16,860
Though I'm pretty sure we can chalk it up to the tireless effort and guidance of your good-natured, beautiful instructor.

62
00:04:19,140 --> 00:04:20,640
I'm so proud of you.

63
00:04:22,180 --> 00:04:23,280
And you too.

64
00:04:27,040 --> 00:04:27,600
Nina!

65
00:04:29,940 --> 00:04:30,960
Oh, Inko!

66
00:04:31,240 --> 00:04:33,240
You guys came back to rescue us!

67
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:36,840
Yeah, but I didn't see your names on any ferry passenger manifest.

68
00:04:37,060 --> 00:04:40,860
That's a relief, huh?

69
00:04:41,060 --> 00:04:41,580
Oh, yeah.

70
00:04:42,660 --> 00:04:43,740
Oh, that's kind of hot.

71
00:04:44,140 --> 00:04:44,500
Ugh.

72
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:46,460
The city.

73
00:04:46,820 --> 00:04:48,100
It's gone now, isn't it?

74
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:49,080
Yeah.

75
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:52,260
Then I would guess that we're next.

76
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:53,080
No way.

77
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:54,940
We're gonna get through this.

78
00:04:55,080 --> 00:04:55,660
Count on it.

79
00:04:55,660 --> 00:05:03,140
If that's the case, then you might want to try not running into that.

80
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:05,620
Right or left or left or right or...

81
00:05:05,620 --> 00:05:06,680
Just vent the skirt.

82
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:15,780
Hey, just what does that helmsman think he's doing?

83
00:05:17,340 --> 00:05:18,120
Pardon me.

84
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:19,600
Yes?

85
00:05:19,900 --> 00:05:21,260
I wanted to thank you.

86
00:05:21,260 --> 00:05:22,260
Uh...

87
00:05:22,260 --> 00:05:23,980
Inaho.

88
00:05:25,180 --> 00:05:26,380
Inaho Kaizuka.

89
00:05:28,220 --> 00:05:30,540
Inaho, my thanks for saving me.

90
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:31,780
My name is...

91
00:05:31,780 --> 00:05:33,740
You can call me Salem.

92
00:05:34,460 --> 00:05:35,780
It's a pleasure to meet you.

93
00:05:37,260 --> 00:05:39,060
Well, thanks, Salem.

94
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:39,880
You too.

95
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:44,180
If you wouldn't mind, perhaps you could show me around this vessel.

96
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:46,180
Hmm.

97
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:49,700
Is that okay?

98
00:05:50,220 --> 00:05:50,560
Mm-hmm.

99
00:05:55,900 --> 00:05:57,400
But, milady, you...

100
00:05:57,400 --> 00:05:58,220
It's all right.

101
00:05:58,220 --> 00:06:05,640
Let's try once more.

102
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:08,380
My name is Asalem vs. Ellusia.

103
00:06:09,100 --> 00:06:11,080
I'm Emperor vs. Granddaughter.

104
00:06:12,840 --> 00:06:15,040
So then, this is the real you?

105
00:06:15,360 --> 00:06:18,040
Before, it was a holographic likeness.

106
00:06:18,300 --> 00:06:19,700
A kind of optical disguise.

107
00:06:19,700 --> 00:06:23,080
But I saw the princess assassinated.

108
00:06:23,660 --> 00:06:25,760
During the parade, I saw the whole thing.

109
00:06:26,600 --> 00:06:27,360
She was...

110
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:28,180
She was a double.

111
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:32,540
Her highness was not well enough to be there as she wished to that day.

112
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:37,220
The security detail leader insisted that her appearances had to be maintained.

113
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:39,720
It really was a double then.

114
00:06:40,220 --> 00:06:43,400
When my grandfather, the Emperor, learns that I am still alive,

115
00:06:43,780 --> 00:06:45,620
this war will come to an immediate end.

116
00:06:46,060 --> 00:06:47,940
So we cannot delay any further.

117
00:06:47,940 --> 00:06:49,840
I must get in touch with Verse.

118
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:51,340
But how?

119
00:06:51,960 --> 00:06:54,200
At this stage, that won't be very easy.

120
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:56,580
They're still jamming our radio signals,

121
00:06:56,580 --> 00:06:59,540
and the Internet's been destroyed along with everything else.

122
00:07:02,420 --> 00:07:07,280
What we can do is take you to a facility where the Verse government can be contacted.

123
00:07:07,860 --> 00:07:09,760
I'll need to speak with my sister, Yuki.

124
00:07:09,980 --> 00:07:11,000
You can't do that!

125
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:14,700
We know that Verse has spies among you that are here on Earth.

126
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:17,080
They had to have worked with the assassins.

127
00:07:17,320 --> 00:07:20,340
Whoever they are, we know they want Her Highness dead.

128
00:07:20,340 --> 00:07:23,800
I'm sorry we have made you a part of this problem.

129
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:25,280
It was not deliberate.

130
00:07:26,900 --> 00:07:27,960
Now I beg you.

131
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:30,980
You must keep this between us.

132
00:07:30,980 --> 00:07:38,200
Oh, I am so glad that we have you here, Dr. Yagarai.

133
00:07:38,580 --> 00:07:43,220
I haven't used servo-assist therapy in a while, so don't try anything out of the ordinary, okay?

134
00:07:43,980 --> 00:07:45,480
Remember, this is only temporary.

135
00:07:45,740 --> 00:07:47,160
Oh, it's fine. This will do.

136
00:07:47,340 --> 00:07:50,060
You may not feel pain now, but it is a strain on your system.

137
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:52,880
When the anesthetic wears off, you'll feel it.

138
00:07:52,980 --> 00:07:54,580
Okay, I've got it. Don't worry.

139
00:07:54,580 --> 00:07:56,880
I'll come in for some fine-tuning later, okay?

140
00:07:57,740 --> 00:07:58,260
Oh.

141
00:07:59,300 --> 00:08:02,200
Or maybe we should take care of those adjustments now.

142
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:08,340
It's sad about Okisuke.

143
00:08:09,340 --> 00:08:11,960
Man, he was a dillweed up to the very end.

144
00:08:12,660 --> 00:08:14,560
Dillweed, pervo, and a slacker.

145
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:17,960
Poor bastard tried to help, but died instead.

146
00:08:18,420 --> 00:08:19,680
And now we dump on him.

147
00:08:20,620 --> 00:08:23,320
Well, he shouldn't have got himself killed.

148
00:08:24,580 --> 00:08:25,100
Inko.

149
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:27,960
They started a war and blew apart our moon.

150
00:08:28,420 --> 00:08:30,880
That Heaven's Fall wrecked the whole damn planet for us.

151
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:34,320
They sit there in the satellite belt looking down on us.

152
00:08:34,840 --> 00:08:39,460
They gotta pay for Okojo and every single person on Earth who's been killed.

153
00:08:39,800 --> 00:08:41,280
Those Martian bastards.

154
00:08:42,800 --> 00:08:46,080
So about earlier, what will you do?

155
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:47,540
Gonna keep her a secret?

156
00:08:48,040 --> 00:08:51,080
When everyone knows an enemy could come at any time,

157
00:08:51,700 --> 00:08:54,160
human beings aren't known for remaining very calm.

158
00:08:54,580 --> 00:08:56,940
If they find out she's a Martian,

159
00:08:57,500 --> 00:08:59,300
no telling what could happen to her.

160
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:03,200
You're a real softie, concerned about the enemy?

161
00:09:04,280 --> 00:09:06,040
She is not our enemy.

162
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:09,760
The enemies are the people who tried to assassinate her.

163
00:09:09,760 --> 00:09:12,780
If what she says is true,

164
00:09:12,780 --> 00:09:17,060
then we've got to get her safely to the United Forces of Earth Headquarters.

165
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:19,520
What about you?

166
00:09:20,020 --> 00:09:20,300
Rye.

167
00:09:20,980 --> 00:09:24,000
My name is Rye Ariash.

168
00:09:24,420 --> 00:09:24,820
Rye.

169
00:09:25,280 --> 00:09:26,420
What are you gonna do?

170
00:09:26,460 --> 00:09:27,160
No guarantees.

171
00:09:27,160 --> 00:09:30,820
If I believe that we're in danger,

172
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:32,940
I'll spill everything.

173
00:09:33,880 --> 00:09:35,220
All Martians are the enemy.

174
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:43,220
Sir Trillram is dead, you say?

175
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:44,520
Yes, my lord.

176
00:09:44,860 --> 00:09:46,160
In the meteor bombardment.

177
00:09:46,420 --> 00:09:47,300
How dare they?

178
00:09:47,560 --> 00:09:51,060
To think a knight would target my territory under the cover of battle.

179
00:09:51,740 --> 00:09:54,600
Have they no honor as orbital knights with a common goal?

180
00:09:54,600 --> 00:10:04,280
In time, I shall learn his identity and then punish him.

181
00:10:05,040 --> 00:10:05,940
Bring Vlad to me.

182
00:10:06,560 --> 00:10:07,740
Hunt down all the Terrans.

183
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,300
Turn this place to ashes.

184
00:10:09,740 --> 00:10:11,140
We shall avenge her highness.

185
00:10:11,400 --> 00:10:11,840
My lord.

186
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:15,440
Um, Princess of Salem is...

187
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:17,020
That's why I'm going to kill her

188
00:10:17,020 --> 00:10:18,880
and make certain of it this time.

189
00:10:18,880 --> 00:10:22,180
What is it?

190
00:10:22,420 --> 00:10:23,720
Well, my lord.

191
00:10:24,380 --> 00:10:26,700
Further devastation to an already conquered area.

192
00:10:27,540 --> 00:10:29,940
Given Princess of Salem's sentiments might...

193
00:10:29,940 --> 00:10:30,360
Wait.

194
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:33,640
Are you implying that you have the right to an opinion?

195
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:34,500
Huh?

196
00:10:37,780 --> 00:10:39,660
Know your place here, Terran.

197
00:10:39,660 --> 00:10:42,820
You think yourself worthy of doing battle for verse?

198
00:10:43,620 --> 00:10:45,640
For 15 long years,

199
00:10:45,780 --> 00:10:48,500
we orbital knights looked out from the shattered moon

200
00:10:48,500 --> 00:10:49,220
to the earth.

201
00:10:49,580 --> 00:10:52,960
Ever yearning for the day we would reach out and take it.

202
00:10:53,720 --> 00:10:54,640
With her death,

203
00:10:54,700 --> 00:10:56,660
our princess made that dream a reality.

204
00:10:57,620 --> 00:10:59,740
This battle belongs to the orbital knights.

205
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:01,400
It does not concern you.

206
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:08,440
He's trying to exploit her death, too.

207
00:11:10,580 --> 00:11:13,960
Ser Trollram was a long-time guest at Castle Cruteo.

208
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:16,640
If we let her stay alive,

209
00:11:16,920 --> 00:11:20,000
my entire clan will surely be branded as traitors!

210
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:21,240
We...

211
00:11:21,240 --> 00:11:23,920
This conspiracy has a ringleader.

212
00:11:25,420 --> 00:11:26,340
Count Cruteo?

213
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,400
No, it can't be.

214
00:11:29,760 --> 00:11:30,760
What do I do?

215
00:11:31,680 --> 00:11:32,820
What do I do?

216
00:11:32,820 --> 00:11:47,940
Power down engines.

217
00:11:48,220 --> 00:11:49,220
Powering down, ma'am.

218
00:11:49,220 --> 00:11:54,440
Captain Margvarege.

219
00:11:54,940 --> 00:11:56,180
I'm glad you're safe.

220
00:11:56,440 --> 00:11:57,360
We've been waiting for you.

221
00:11:57,560 --> 00:11:58,600
Commander Nakabayashi.

222
00:11:58,860 --> 00:11:59,660
Good to see you, sir.

223
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:01,140
Where's everyone else?

224
00:12:01,580 --> 00:12:04,980
The assault craft Watatsumi is currently taking a longer, safer route.

225
00:12:05,400 --> 00:12:06,400
The seas are a mess,

226
00:12:06,740 --> 00:12:09,000
thanks to that unexpected meteor bombardment.

227
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:11,480
On Exo Mizusaki's orders,

228
00:12:11,740 --> 00:12:14,340
we went ahead in landing craft one with Appaloosa platoon.

229
00:12:15,180 --> 00:12:19,800
We are here to give you support and defend the refugees until the Watatsumi arrives.

230
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:21,220
That's a big help.

231
00:12:22,100 --> 00:12:23,360
This place was abandoned.

232
00:12:23,620 --> 00:12:23,760
Hmm?

233
00:12:24,560 --> 00:12:27,860
Even though there isn't much evidence of damage to the general area.

234
00:12:28,980 --> 00:12:29,540
Yes, ma'am.

235
00:12:30,320 --> 00:12:31,420
A wise decision.

236
00:12:32,380 --> 00:12:34,780
Digging in only makes damages worse later.

237
00:12:35,180 --> 00:12:36,540
Makes sense to get out of here.

238
00:12:36,540 --> 00:12:41,860
That's what I'd expect to hear from someone who lived through the war 15 years ago.

239
00:12:43,160 --> 00:12:45,280
We'll wait for the Watatsumi to arrive.

240
00:12:46,360 --> 00:12:49,200
Volunteer some hands to help with resupplying the landing craft.

241
00:12:49,640 --> 00:12:50,060
Understood.

242
00:12:51,380 --> 00:12:51,540
Hmm.

243
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,900
I'm gonna put these rations here.

244
00:13:02,100 --> 00:13:02,680
Thank you.

245
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:06,080
Wow, we're not accustomed to seeing you help out like this, Calm.

246
00:13:06,080 --> 00:13:09,040
Yeah, when we were doing military drills, you were always gone.

247
00:13:09,300 --> 00:13:09,620
Yeah.

248
00:13:09,980 --> 00:13:10,940
Well, that was then.

249
00:13:11,260 --> 00:13:13,940
Now we'll do anything if it means wiping out the Martians.

250
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:17,180
I've scheduled us for a three-shift perimeter watch.

251
00:13:17,320 --> 00:13:18,780
Did the Watatsumi check in yet?

252
00:13:18,980 --> 00:13:19,980
They can't get through.

253
00:13:20,200 --> 00:13:21,320
Jamming is too intense.

254
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:24,180
We can't get a signal within a few dozen miles.

255
00:13:24,500 --> 00:13:26,080
We'll continue scanning for anything.

256
00:13:26,080 --> 00:13:26,180
Okay.

257
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:38,660
Appaloosa leader, this is Appaloosa 3-3.

258
00:13:38,980 --> 00:13:40,200
We've got a friendly here.

259
00:13:40,600 --> 00:13:41,880
Looks like there's some damage.

260
00:13:42,400 --> 00:13:42,620
Huh?

261
00:13:44,620 --> 00:13:46,380
Appaloosa 3-3, report!

262
00:13:46,900 --> 00:13:47,700
What's that?

263
00:13:47,700 --> 00:13:59,540
It's an attack!

264
00:14:03,660 --> 00:14:04,940
What the hell?

265
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:10,160
All hands, battle stations.

266
00:14:10,360 --> 00:14:10,920
Yes, ma'am.

267
00:14:11,460 --> 00:14:13,380
Prep LC-1 for immediate launch.

268
00:14:13,540 --> 00:14:14,960
Everyone, get inside!

269
00:14:14,960 --> 00:14:20,720
Appaloosa 3-3, report!

270
00:14:21,500 --> 00:14:24,540
Enemy cataphract, single unit, bunker behind a building.

271
00:14:24,860 --> 00:14:25,780
